      "id": "lem-riesz-transform-kernels-have-explicit-size-difference-and-spherical-cancellation-bounds",
      "location": "Statement",
      "defect": "false-claim",
      "evidence": "The Statement gives “C_n:=c_n 2^{n+1}(3n+4)” and says “at n=1 it reads C_1=14c_1=14/π.” Substituting n=1 in the displayed formula gives 28c_1; the in-scope Riesz definition gives c_1=1/π, so the parenthetical value should be 28/π.",
      "severity": "fatal",
      "observed_sha256": "366b1a8d130572b74a3651470fa2a905391fd7774878ea1132773184302302eb"
    },
    {
      "obligation": "refuter:11:2",
      "id": "lem-riesz-transform-principal-value-kernel-formula",
      "location": "Proof 1.1",
      "defect": "unlicensed-inference",
      "evidence": "The proof says Schwartz decay makes “|K_j(y)f(x-y)|≤c_nC_{n+2}(f)|y|^{-n-2}” on |y|>1. The cited Schwartz bound controls f(z) by C_{n+2}(f)(1+|z|)^{-n-2}; setting z=x-y does not yield decay in |y| with that same constant uniformly in x. For f(z)=e^{-|z|^2}, x=y=Re_j gives a left side c_nR^{-n}, which exceeds c_nC_{n+2}(f)R^{-n-2} for sufficiently large R. The tail is integrable for each fixed x, but this displayed estimate needs an x-dependent translated Schwartz bound or a compact-tail split.",
      "severity": "nonfatal",
      "observed_sha256": "f0473db83dc55442c36630288863d68b19cddca95fca6efa959d3daa5de985c4"
    },
    {
      "obligation": "refuter:11:3",
      "id": "lem-singular-kernel-sine-integral-under-countable-choice",
      "location": "Proof 7.1",
      "defect": "unlicensed-inference",
      "evidence": "The proof applies the substitution “u=|z|t” for every real z. Its cited change-of-variable result requires a monotone differentiable surjection; when z=0 this map is constant and does not satisfy that hypothesis. The displayed identity at z=0 is true directly, since the integrand is zero, but that case is not justified by the stated substitution.",
      "severity": "nonfatal",
      "observed_sha256": "970529379bbe9c7fa40316ad0ed5c4bc37441da0b3f09ceba9a8c9708f2397de"
    }
  ],
